---
/**
 * KatexStyles.astro : opt-in KaTeX CSS bundle.
 *
 * v9.2.2 (Gate 12) : Phase 5a fix. The KaTeX minified CSS (≈24 KB
 * + 25 @font-face rules for math glyphs) was previously imported
 * eagerly in BaseLayout.astro, so every page in the site paid the
 * full cost on first paint. Only `Equation.astro` and `Stat.astro`
 * actually render KaTeX at runtime, so the CSS is moved here and
 * imported by those two components. Vite's chunking puts the CSS
 * into a per-page bundle only for pages that import Equation/Stat;
 * pages that don't (home, /for-recruiters, /screening-call, etc.)
 * get zero KaTeX bytes on the critical path.
 *
 * Why not async-load from the layout: the CSS @font-face rules
 * point at relative woff/ttf URLs; if the rule is missing when the
 * browser encounters a `.katex` element the user sees a flash of
 * unstyled math glyphs. Bundling the CSS with the consumer is
 * the only correctness-preserving split.
 *
 * Body is empty : pure side-effect import. Astro/Vite tree-shake
 * this for pages that don't transitively import Equation/Stat.
 */
import 'katex/dist/katex.min.css';
